### Bluetooth audio for d2s: BlueZ's own headset backend, NOT the droid one.
###
### default_sailfish.pa includes this file in place of its own
###     load-module module-bluez5-discover headset=droid enable_msbc=false
### line, the same hook arm_droid_card_custom.pa uses for the card.
###
### `headset=droid` routes HSP/HFP through the droid audio HAL, by way of
### module-droid-glue. On this device that backend has nothing behind it:
### module-droid-card is not loaded at all (see arm_droid_card_custom.pa - the
### only real audio HAL is 32-bit and a 64-bit PulseAudio cannot dlopen it), and
### module-droid-glue.so is not even installed. PulseAudio still took the droid
### path whenever a Bluetooth audio device was connected.
###
### Observed with a headset connected and the volume changed from the top menu:
### PulseAudio died with SIGSEGV twice in one session, taking jolla-settings
### with it (SIGABRT) when its D-Bus calls went unanswered, while the policy
### logged
###     policy-group.c: pa_policy_group_move_to(): could not find sink for type
###     ihf name (null)
###     dbusif.c: Got 2 routing decisions. 1 decisions were incomplete.
###
### `native` is PulseAudio's own SCO backend and needs no droid HAL. Bluetooth
### audio still does not play on this port - nothing switches the route to a
### Bluetooth sink - but connecting a device and changing the volume no longer
### takes the audio stack down with it.
###
### enable_msbc stays false, as in the line this replaces.
load-module module-bluez5-discover headset=native enable_msbc=false
